# --- More than one account per vendor -------------------------------------
#
# ZYTE_API_KEY, APIFY_TOKEN, SERPAPI_KEY and OXYLABS_USERNAME/PASSWORD each
# accept extra accounts as numbered siblings, handed out round robin so the
# vendor's ceiling is the sum of the accounts rather than one of them:
#
#     SERPAPI_KEY=first
#     SERPAPI_KEY_2=second
#     SERPAPI_KEY_3=third
#
# Oxylabs pairs positionally: OXYLABS_USERNAME_2 goes with OXYLABS_PASSWORD_2.
# Numbered rather than comma-separated because two of these are passwords, and
# any delimiter is a character some password contains. Adding none of them
# behaves exactly as a single key always did. GET /api/health reports how many
# accounts each vendor loaded — check it after adding one, because an account
# that failed to load looks identical to one that is working, only slower.
#
# What this does and does not buy: it raises quota and rate ceilings. It does
# NOT make one search faster — the Lens pass already runs every product at once
# against a single key. The knobs that change wall-clock time are the frontend's
# PREFETCH_PARALLEL and the Browserbase plan behind it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ZYTE_API_KEY=ecb8ab17d4d048049afab19461d20f38
APIFY_TOKEN=apify_api_RO9O6p4qTyG1F5EcjBs8TbyCdZSlLm2CqsdI
PINTEREST_ACTOR=fetch_cat~pinterest-search-scraper
CAPSOLVER_API_KEY=CAP-315E4292BC9F2E20616B7192EE6469DF6DAD218855514B0B7ABB371BCC0D2C1F
TWOCAPTCHA_API_KEY=c88f7968baa01d26c25176fb0252ab6b

